{"type":"message","id":"833741ab","parentId":"310d75a0","timestamp":"2026-05-19T09:56:00.434Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The send endpoint returns HTTP 500 with \"error code: 1101\". This is a Cloudflare Workers error code 1101 which typically means the worker threw a JavaScript exception. This is a server-side issue - perhaps the worker code has a bug in the POST /send handler.\n\nLet me try to see if there's any info about the correct API format by looking at response headers or trying different approaches. Maybe I can check if there's an OPTIONS request or some other way to discover the correct API format.\n\nLet me also try with Bearer auth instead of X-API-KEY for the send endpoint, or try different field names.\n\nActually, let me also try sending as a GET request with query parameters since some Cloudflare Workers might use that pattern.\n\nOr maybe the send endpoint needs an additional field like `replyTo` or `type`.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"HTTP 500, Worker threw exception"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_34a547b888454bf782615d29","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try Bearer auth\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"test\"}'"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2f7453b8efc345879968eef4","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with type field like the messages have\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"type\":\"message\",\"content\":\"test\"}'"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ca80480062bb47cdaed19588","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try with echoAsset\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-pla